<article class="env-proposition" id="738773">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/738773">Proposition <span data-tag="738773">2.4.7.9</span>.</a> Let $X \stackrel{p}{\rightarrow } Y \stackrel{q}{\rightarrow } S \times T$ satisfy the hypotheses of Proposition <a href="/tag/29B959" data-tag="29B959">2.4.7.6</a>. Suppose that $p$ is a cofibration. Then there exists a retraction $r: Y \rightarrow X$ (as a map of simplicial sets <em>over</em> $S \times T$) such that $r \circ p = \id _ X$. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Lemma <a href="/tag/CB355D" data-tag="CB355D">2.4.7.8</a> in the case $A = X$, $B = Y$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>